b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for or take care of a child as appropriate, carried out by parents, guardians or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a wife within the scope of her household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or because of an agreement or contract, he is obliged to provide a living, care or maintenance to his wife; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence, by restricting and/or prohibiting a wife from working properly inside or outside the home so that the wife is under the control of her husband.

